# Skip Unchanged Edit Form Updates

Edit/save handlers must **not** call update/PUT mutations when the submitted
values are equivalent to the loaded entity.

## Required pattern

1. Convert the loaded entity with the feature `*ToFormValues` helper (or a
   feature-specific normalizer).
2. Compare with `areXFormValuesEquivalent` (preferred) or shared
   `areFormValuesEquivalent` from `@/lib/forms/are-form-values-equivalent`.
3. On match: toast `t("common.form.noChanges")`, close the form tab/dialog, and
   **return without calling the mutation**.

```tsx
// ✅ GOOD
if (isEditing && editing) {
  if (areItemFormValuesEquivalent(values, itemToFormValues(editing))) {
    notifySuccess(t("common.form.noChanges"));
    closeFormTabAndReturn(tabId);
    return;
  }
  await updateMutation.mutateAsync({ itemId: editing.itemId, values });
}
```

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — always PUTs even when nothing changed
if (isEditing && editing) {
  await updateMutation.mutateAsync({ itemId: editing.itemId, values });
}
```

## Where helpers live

- Shared: `src/lib/forms/are-form-values-equivalent.ts`
- Feature wrappers next to `*ToFormValues` in `src/lib/<feature>/types.ts`
  (e.g. `areCustomerFormValuesEquivalent` may normalize before compare)
- Locale: `common.form.noChanges` in both `en` and `es` `common.json`

## Scope

- Apply to desktop form tabs (`*-form-workspace.tsx`) **and** directory dialog
  save handlers (`*-workspace.tsx`).
- Apply per independent edit section (e.g. daily income statement vs journal).
- Create paths stay unchanged — only skip update/PUT.
